This equation is fundamentally a relationship between operators in quantum mechanics and does not typically exhibit limits in the same way as classical physical quantities. However, its utility depends on the domain of the wavefunction. In the limit of very high momentum (
$$p \to \infty$$
) or very low momentum (
$$p \to 0$$
), the differential nature of the position operator remains, but the interpretation of the resulting quantum state's spatial characteristics will depend on the specific wavefunction being acted upon.

