The Hubble parameter, denoted by H, represents the rate of expansion of the universe. It is defined as the ratio of the time derivative of the scale factor to the scale factor itself. It is often expressed in units of km/s/Mpc, but in fundamental equations, its SI unit is inverse seconds (s
<sup>-1</sup>
).
